extraction_notes: "WB30 D-Bees of North America printed 185-188 (cache p186-p189, cache page = printed + 1). Read off 200 dpi renders; lore 185-186, the R.C.C. block 186-188, ending with the Note above the Simvan Monster Riders heading on 188. A reprint (the entry cites Rifts Sourcebook One); the catalog held no shemarrian class on 2026-10-03. Tag line: Shemarrian Warrior - Optional Player Character and NPC (playable at the GM''s discretion, which the restriction line states). || CATEGORY: a robot R.C.C. that takes no O.C.C.; main body M.D.C. 400 in armor is mdc_base (no men_of_arms line). No occ_restrictions block, following the other no-O.C.C. races; it is a restriction line. || XP: the book says use the same experience table as the Dragon Hatchling. By the 2026-09-26 copy rule (class-import reference, xp_table), copied from the stored dragon-hatchling ladder (Rifts Ultimate Edition). || ATTRIBUTES: fixed figures stored as fixed attribute_dice: I.Q. 14 (Neural Intelligence), M.A. effectively 1D6, P.S. 36 (Robot), P.P. 24, P.B. 24, Spd 132 (90 mph/144 km). M.E. and P.E. are printed not applicable and are not stored. P.P.E. -0- stored as 0. Horror Factor not applicable; no key. No hit points or S.D.C. are printed. || ATTACKS: printed Eight, stored as attacks_base 8 with ignores_style_attacks, since the figure is the robot''s whole count. || BONUSES (in addition to attributes and skills) as printed: +3 initiative, +7 strike, +9 parry and dodge, +5 pull punch/claw (pull_punch), +4 roll with impact. Critical strike on 19-20 and the +6 rail gun / +4 other ranged strike bonuses are a special ability; Paired Weapons is the skill. || SKILLS: the book gives the A-64 Master''s skill programs and refers to Rifts Sourcebook One Revised for specifics; stored is what this page prints. Basic Math (96%) as Mathematics: Basic 96. All Military, Espionage and Scouting skills (+40%) is stored as every catalog Military row (24) and Espionage row (14) on 2026-10-03, each at catalog base +40, capped at 98 where that passes 98 (Demolitions, Demolitions Disposal, Make and Modify Weapons, Modify Weapon Cartridges) and per_level 0 there; Forced March and Sniper carry no percentage. Scouting is not a catalog category and is not stored. W.P. Energy Pistol, Energy Rifle, Heavy M.D. Weapons, Blunt, Chain, Knife, Sword and Paired Weapons as printed. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts at 8th level proficiency is the skill with the level in its note (the proficiency level is not stored as a number; the eight attacks are attacks_base). No hand_to_hand block: no change or price is printed. Dragonese 98% as Language: Dragonese 98; the 92% languages and Splugorth 80% are the Speech ability (no Splugorth row). || EQUIPMENT: backpack, large sack, belts (Utility Belt), cloak (Hooded Cloak), Vibro-Knife, Vibro-Sword, one energy pistol and one energy rifle of choice (the usual catalog choice sets) and 1D6 E-Clips for each (two entries of 1D6). The Shemarrian Rail Gun has no catalog row and is a special ability with its printed stats (not stubbed); personal items not stored. || MONEY: 2D6x1,000 credits taken from slavers. || NOT STORED: size 8 feet, weight 900 lbs, life span (not alive; power supply replaced every 20 years or so), slave market value at least 4D6x10,000, habitat, allies and enemies are in GM Notes."
