## Lore

Shemarrians pass as a race of tall, beautiful warrior women from beyond the
Rifts, part woman and part bionic machine. In truth they are androids built by
Archie Three and Hagan Lonovich: a human-looking head and face over a bulky
robot body, made lovely on purpose so that foes hesitate and bystanders are
slow to destroy them.

Their programming gives them simulated emotions and an invented history of an
alien homeland. They are cold, stern and proud, take on duels to prove they are
the finest warriors alive, and look down on weak humans and most D-Bees. They
fight slavers, free captives and wage a guerrilla war on the Horune Pirates and
the Minions of Splugorth along the Atlantic coast, which has made them heroes to
the wilderness folk of the Northeast. Lord Splynncryth has no idea who is really
behind them.

A Shemarrian played as a character is not a simple machine but a thinking
android. She may start as Archie''s rigid servant and, over time and in the
company of others, begin to think and feel for herself. Archie, who likes to
think of himself as a god, is inclined to let her.

## GM Notes

Size 8 feet (2.4 m). Weight 900 pounds (405 kg). Not alive: an undamaged unit
could run for decades with its nuclear power supply replaced or recharged every
20 years or so. Anyone who can Object Read or communicate with machines learns
by touch that the women and their mounts are robots, with a vision of a dark
factory and a helmeted man on a throne.

Habitat: the Atlantic Northeast from West Virginia to Newfoundland and west to
the Appalachians, occasionally anywhere in North America. Slave market value at
least 4D6x10,000 credits, though none has ever been enslaved. Allies: none as
such, but respected by the people they protect along the East Coast; Faerie Bot
D-Bees know the truth and keep it secret. Enemies: the Minions of Splugorth,
Horune Pirates and all slavers; wary of Free Quebec and CS soldiers; distrust
magic and all who use it.

The entry first appeared in Rifts Sourcebook One; Rifts Sourcebook One,
Revised and Expanded has more on the Shemarrians, their Monst-Rex mounts and
Archie''s other robots.
